ivities S, we must schedule them all using the minimum number of rooms.\n\nGreedy1: Use the optimal algorithm for the Activity Selection Problem to find the max number of activities that can be scheduled in one room. Delete and repeat on the rest, until no activities left.\n\nGreedy2:\n- Sort activities by start time. Open room 1 for"},{"type":"image","src":"../../assets/0a8e764fa43fe6205585a37a13a2b686bb031ffefd5d85b1f4fbc66329b2b4cc.png"},{"type":"text","content":".\n- for i=2 to n if"},{"type":"image","src":"../../assets/323c3d4c1fdb136520af119a69c52a16d95d40e22c995072cefc4e7ce601b24d.png"},{"type":"text","content":"can fit in any open room, schedule it in that room; otherwise open a new room for"},{"type":"image","src":"../../assets/323c3d4c1fdb136520af119a69c52a16d95d40e22c995072cefc4e7ce601b24d.png"},{"type":"text","content":".\n\nWhich of the following statements is correct?"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"None of the above two greedy algorithms are optimal.","correct":false,"option_id":"b0ca838c-d885-4ebc-a5ae-9e16cb11ec62"},{"type":"text","content":"Greedy1 is an optimal algorithm and Greedy2 is not.","correct":false,"option_id":"db7ecc79-394e-4027-9ac9-dd069d807adc"},{"type":"text","content":"Greedy2 is an optimal algorithm and Greedy1 is not.","correct":true,"option_id":"2511dd87-d7e3-4331-abdb-87ef422a58d8"},{"type":"text","content":"Both of the above two greedy algorithms are optimal.","correct":false,"option_id":"ddbfccdb-8341-4dcf-bbfe-6e01b40674d1"}]}}},{"path":"versions/de94110b-f99d-4e88-b440-2a0260dbf079/e47b66356c32df5a2f5f1f2d2731efeb13daf25a423609a55ee3357ff7bed7da.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"de94110b-f99d-4e88-b440-2a0260dbf079","revision":"sha256:e47b66356c32df5a2f5f1f2d2731efeb13daf25a423609a55ee3357ff7bed7da","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Let S be the set of activities in Activity Selection Problem. Then there must be some maximum-size subset of mutually compatible activities of S that includes the earliest finish activity."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"317d37e8-b03e-48ae-8f60-1a3d60d89a8e"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"52b335d6-2748-4997-a2f7-87b2e75d6fc4"}]}}},{"path":"versions/ade33940-2a91-45f0-9be8-881fc504fee4/db19afa56d0dfb11c67aee0f85ac7fe16e399839c12b2a1480e531019f8c32bc.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"ade33940-2a91-45f0-9be8-881fc504fee4","revision":"sha256:db19afa56d0dfb11c67aee0f85ac7fe16e399839c12b2a1480e531019f8c32bc","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Given 4 cases of frequences of four characters. In which case(s) that the total bits taken by Huffman codes are the same as that of the ordinary equal length codes?\n\n\n(1) 4 2 11 6\n(2) 6 5 7 12\n(3) 3 2 3 4\n(4) 8 3 10 7"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"(3) only","correct":false,"option_id":"9f49eda4-8736-4969-bad9-4f54f3434949"},{"type":"text","content":"(1) and (3)","correct":false,"option_id":"eaa5f7b0-aa15-41c6-8d8b-5d2d69c064e3"},{"type":"text","content":"(3) and (4)","correct":true,"option_id":"56554cea-6c6b-423b-b10f-2009331c45be"},{"type":"text","content":"none","correct":false,"option_id":"601bd458-2953-402d-b47e-6abbe8aa7973"}]}}},{"path":"versions/862343fb-cd4c-47ea-91f4-2b068058f7e1/fe1852385624a264e529c5a73cfb5551e225bf6c73241fd2febe945cf3e9422b.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"862343fb-cd4c-47ea-91f4-2b068058f7e1","revision":"sha256:fe1852385624a264e529c5a73cfb5551e225bf6c73241fd2febe945cf3e9422b","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Given four characters (a, b, c, d) with distinct frequencies in a text. Suppose that a and b are the two characters having the lowest frequencies. Which of the following sets of code is a possible Huffman code for this text?"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"a: 000, b:001, c:01, d:1","correct":true,"option_id":"54a69cec-21f9-479d-9249-0ec01fb8ccb7"},{"type":"text","content":"a: 000, b:001, c:01, d:11","correct":false,"option_id":"4d873569-9f5c-430d-a650-c0e1da5c6d97"},{"type":"text","content":"a: 000, b:001, c:10, d:1","correct":false,"option_id":"40fa9f28-9893-45de-a3b4-81464a3cbf2d"},{"type":"text","content":"a: 010, b:001, c:01, d:1","correct":false,"option_id":"3e9304da-ad75-49f5-a134-aa2654ab55ed"}]}}}]}